*.local
*.identcache
*.projdata
*.tvsconfig
*.dsk
*.dsm

# Delphi history and backups
__history/
# RAD Studio's crash-recovery copies, same class as __history: editor state,
# not source.  Committed by accident in 75ce5a60 via `git add <dir>`.
__recovery/
*.~*
# The IDE's previous-version copy, rewritten on every save.  One of these
# (LOGRADIO.$$$) was tracked and showed as modified forever, with 600-line
# diffs that were pure noise against the .PAS beside it.
*.$$$

# Castalia statistics file
*.stat.gitignore

*.ini
tr4w/target/tr4w.exe
tr4w/target/settings/TR4W.INI
*.pos
*.CFG
*.map
tr4w/target/tr4w.map
tr4w/target/tr4w-debug.log
tr4w/target/tr4w.log
# Ignore everything in target/ but allow specific tracked subdirectories/files.
# Must use tr4w/target/* (not tr4w/target/) so git descends into the directory
# and honours the negation rules below. A trailing-slash ignore pattern causes
# git to skip the directory entirely, making negations inside it ineffective.
#
# cty.dat note: the file IS tracked in master (so fresh clones get a working
# copy), but it is intentionally NOT re-included via negation here.  TR4W
# rewrites cty.dat at runtime; we no longer want those local edits to surface
# in `git status` or be accidentally committed.  Each developer should also
# run `git update-index --skip-worktree tr4w/target/cty.dat` once locally to
# fully silence cty.dat from status.  If the master copy ever genuinely needs
# updating, `git add -f tr4w/target/cty.dat` bypasses this ignore.
tr4w/target/*
!tr4w/target/dom
!tr4w/target/trcluster.dat
!tr4w/target/commands*.ini
tr4w/tr4w.cfg
tr4w/tr4w.dof
# Generated each build by FullBuild.ps1 Write-VersionInfoResource: a
# language- and version-specific VERSIONINFO PE resource picked up by
# tr4w.dpr via {$IFDEF VERSIONINFO_RES}{$R tr4w_versioninfo.res}{$ENDIF}.
# Files never need to be tracked -- always regenerated.
tr4w/tr4w_versioninfo.rc
tr4w/tr4w_versioninfo.res
tr4w/COMPILER.LOG
tr4w/tr4w.log
*.RST
*.TRW
*.LOG

# ADIF exports. The program writes these constantly -- /EXPORT mode, the Post
# menu, and every corpus run -- and they are operating data, not source. A
# 375 KB log.ADI sat untracked in a corpus set on 2026-08-26 because the root
# had no rule at all and the corpus subtree re-includes *.ADI wholesale.
#
# THE CURATED FIXTURES ARE THE EXCEPTION, and they re-include themselves in
# their own subtree: tr4w/test/corpus/.gitignore (the 13 ref.adi golden
# masters) and tr4w/test/unit/fixtures/.gitignore (the 11 parser fixtures).
# Add a new one there and it is tracked normally; drop a stray export
# anywhere and it stays out.
*.adi
*.ADI

# Build output text files
tr4w/build_*.txt
tr4w/COMPILATION_RESULTS.txt
tr4w/compile_*.txt
tr4w/tr4w.log.*
tr4w/build_*.log

# CLAUDE CODE: project guardrails are TRACKED, personal config is not.
#
# .claude/ was ignored wholesale until 2026-08-29, which meant every hook this
# repo relies on -- the git -C rule, the Pascal glob rule, the begin/end lint,
# the CRLF check -- existed on one machine and nowhere else, and CLAUDE.md
# described a settings.json that was not in the repository at all.
#
# Ignore everything under .claude/, then re-include the two things that belong
# to the PROJECT rather than to the developer. Order matters: negations must
# follow the blanket rule, and git cannot re-include a path through an ignored
# parent directory -- which is why the blanket is ".claude/*" and not ".claude/".
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/

# commands/ joined the tracked set on 2026-08-30: /update-changes and
# /monthly-changes were ported from the D7 tree, where they had lived on one
# machine only. A slash command that exists in a single clone is the same
# problem the hooks had before they were tracked.

# skills/ joined on 2026-08-31, and the reason is the same one again. A
# /doctor pass moved the 2026-08-19 history-rewrite forensics and the
# stale-clone reset recipe OUT of CLAUDE.md and into
# .claude/skills/git-history-recovery/, leaving a pointer behind. With
# .claude/skills ignored that pointer would have resolved on exactly one
# machine while the content it names was deleted everywhere -- a dangling
# reference in the file people trust most, which is worse than the long
# section it replaced.
tr4w/.claude/

# Personal, machine-specific, or scratch. Never tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.bak-*
.claude/worktrees/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Network capture files (local debugging only)
*.pcap
*.pcapng

# GitHub Wiki — separate repo at n4af/TR4W.wiki.git, cloned locally for editing
wiki/
pcap/
spike/units/
spike/units_indy/
spike/*.exe
spike/*.o
spike/*.ppu
spike/*.exe
spike/units/


