# handed out per rig, not release history. The release itself is a tag.
tr4w/build/release/*.zip
tr4w/build/release/README_*.txt

# FPC sweep reports -- generated artifacts, regenerate with spike/fpc-sweep.ps1
spike/sweep-*.txt
spike/units/

# LCL probe build artefacts
spike/lclprobe/*.exe
spike/lclprobe/*.o
spike/lclprobe/*.or
spike/lclprobe/*.ppu

# Lint-LFMProperties compiles its checker on demand (build\lintlfm\lintlfm.lpr);
# the .ppu/.o/.exe are build output, not source.
tr4w/build/lintlfm/units/

# FPC intermediate output (units, logs). Binaries land in target\ and tr4wserver\.
build-out/

# Lazarus SESSION state -- open tabs, cursor positions, breakpoints, watches.
# Per-developer and rewritten on every close; the PROJECT file (.lpi) is
# tracked and must stay so, since it carries the search paths and the
# debug settings.
*.lps

# Release symbols: ~46 MB per build, kept beside the installer so an emailed
# crash address can be resolved later. Never committed -- archive with the
# release artefacts instead.
tr4w/build/release/symbols/

# Raw contest logs and cluster captures that NO automated test reads -- 53 MB:
# 37 D7-era log sets kept as a source for building NEW corpus sets by hand (the
# D12_ROOT flow in tr4w/test/corpus/corpus-lib.sh), and dxcluster/, 209 captured
# sessions used by hand when changing spot column/comment logic.  The 13 sets
# the corpus exercises are staged from their own tracked log.cfg/log.trw, and
# uTestDXSpotParse carries its sample lines inline, so this directory can be
# absent and the corpus still runs 22/0/4 from a fresh clone.
corpus_test_data/local_test_data/

# Lazarus form backups. The IDE writes the PREVIOUS revision of a form into a
# backup/ folder beside it on every save, so these are stale by definition and
# nothing compiles them. Lint-FormOverlap already skips the directory for the
# same reason -- a stale layout failing the build is a false alarm about a file
# nothing builds.
#
# 74 of them were committed by accident on 2026-08-26 by staging the directory
# rather than the files.
tr4w/src/ui/lcl/backup/

# The PROJECT backup directory, same mechanism one level up: Lazarus writes the
# previous revision of tr4w.lpi/.lpr here on every save, so tr4w/backup/tr4w.lpi
# showed as modified after each time the IDE was opened.
#
# tr4w.dpr and tr4w.lpi were committed here by accident in adaa30dd, the .dpr ->
# .lpr rename. Nothing is lost by untracking them: the pre-rename program file is
# git show adaa30dd^:tr4w/tr4w.dpr, and a stale copy of a file that HAS moved is
# worse than no copy -- the sibling directory already proved that, where a grep
# for tDialogBox found the pre-conversion uLogCompareForm and had to be filtered
# out by hand every time.
tr4w/backup/

# Defuzzed test catalogues (tools/i18n/po_defuzz.py). They carry UNREVIEWED
# machine translation for layout testing and must never be shipped or committed.
build-out/**/languages/
tr4w/src/*.tmp
tr4w/res/RCa*

# Poedit compiles a .mo beside the .po; the binary is build output, not source.
i18n/*.mo
# Lazarus copies the loaded application icon beside the project when you use
# Project Options -> Application -> Load Icon. It is a byte-identical copy of
# tr4w/res/tr4w.ico, which is the tracked source, and the icon the build links
# comes from tr4w.res -- so this is a third copy of the same image and exactly
# the kind of duplicate that drifts.
tr4w/tr4w.ico
